# What is published is just what is needed to run the emulator without recompiling it: the .exe in the root,
# datos/ with what it reads, launcher_assets/, docs/ and the source code. Everything else out.

# ─── Build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
publish/
runtimes/
*.pdb
*.deps.json
*.runtimeconfig.json
# The dlls go inside the single-file .exe; none loose.
*.dll

# ─── Databases ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# world.db is 240 MB: it is distributed compressed in datos/world.zip and the emulator extracts it on its own
# the first time. auth.db it creates itself with its test account.
bases/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# ─── Data extracted from the client ─────────────────────────────────────────
# 436 MB of raw dump. It is not needed to run: what the emulator reads is already in
# datos/, and tools/ generates it from this folder.
dofus3_data/
Dofus3 Defuscated Data/
DofusClient/

# ─── Tools ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Python scripts generate the json files of datos/ and audit the traffic. They are not needed to
# run the emulator.
tools/
*.py
__pycache__/

# ─── Logs and captures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never. They carry real account names.
logs/
*.log
*.csv
*.pcapng
*.hex

# ─── Data the emulator does not read ────────────────────────────────────────
# They are on disk for reference, but Paths does not resolve them.
datos/world_entering_3_6_10_10.bin
datos/characteristics.json
datos/dofus3_mappings.json
datos/effects.json
# map_neighbours.json IS read since 27/08/2026: it is what gives Jondo Studio the four
# neighbouring maps, which is how the world is really walked instead of by eight-digit
# ids. It is 2.6 MB and it is the only file this change adds to the repository.

# ─── Leftovers from earlier versions ────────────────────────────────────────
# The technical specification is a 3,893-line chronicle of how each thing was discovered,
# carried over from version 3.6.4.3. It is valuable to whoever wrote it, but it is not a
# reference and it mixes things that no longer hold, so it stays local and is not published. What
# is useful to look up is in the other documents of docs/.
docs/EspecificacionTecnica.md
# And this is not Jondo documentation: it is the README of UnityInspectorStandalone, an external
# tool used to inspect the client at run time. It stays local as a working
# reference, but in the repository it only misleads.
docs/UnityInspectorReadme.md
out.txt
mock_server.db
*_old.cs
scratch_*

# ─── Development environments ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

# ─── Deobfuscator ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The model's answers are a cache: they can be asked for again, they take a file per question and
# say nothing that is not already in datos/propuestas_*.tsv. The dossiers are 2,169 files that
# «expediente --todos» regenerates in a second from the index.
datos/respuestas/
expedientes/

# ─── Clients downloaded from the CDN ────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cytrus manifests are 51 MB per version and are pure cache: «protocolbuilder bajar» fetches
# them again, and checks each file against its hash. The clients themselves are 183 MB per
# version and are not published either: they are Ankama's.
datos/cytrus/
clientes/

# The tests project builds like any other
TestResults/
Jondo.Unity.Tests/bin/
Jondo.Unity.Tests/obj/
Jondo.Unity.Studio/bin/
Jondo.Unity.Studio/obj/

# The photos of the launcher window: they are working files, not part of the project.
capturas-lanzador/
README.bbcode.txt
